#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188065 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188357 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91379d24-6b6d-5642-8eb8-cbcc8feaf355" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum or Difference of Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "7ea98738-258e-5cc4-9e04-58b0b4638290" :question/math-academy-id "e-10435" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 3,$ $\\textrm{Var}[Y] = 0.24,$ and $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 0.2.$ Determine $\\textrm{Var}[X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X \\pm Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y] \\pm 2\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X - Y] = 3 + 0.24 - 2 \\cdot 0.2 = 2.84.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188067 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188359 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96172470-bd90-53eb-aea7-87d08f462ea2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Scaled Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "0bc5206c-e880-5016-9653-49ac54af4d2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-10443" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 5,$ $\\textrm{Var}[Y] = 2,$ and $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 3.$ Find $\\textrm{Var}[2X - 5Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX + bY] = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2ab\\,\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-5Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-5)^{2}\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =20+50-60 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188068 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39efc83e-6658-5b7a-979b-dbc35af5dd98" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Moments"}] :question/id #uuid "04bff442-bf0b-529b-a8d8-14538a1db48f" :question/math-academy-id "e-10444" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{Var}[5X+2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+bY] = a^2 \\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2 \\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2ab\\,\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm{E}[X^2] - \\textrm{E}[X]^2,\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = \\textrm{E}[XY] - \\textrm{E}[X] \\cdot \\textrm{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\textrm{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space $S_X,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.4+3\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =1.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.4+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =5.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5.4-{1.8}^{2} \\\\  & =2.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space $S_Y,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\textrm{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot f(0,0)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+3\\cdot 0\\cdot f(3,0)+3\\cdot 2\\cdot f(3,2) \\\\  & =0+0+0+6\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =1.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.2-1.8\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[5X+2Y] & ={5}^{2}\\cdot 2.16+{2}^{2}\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 5\\cdot 2\\cdot (-0.6) \\\\  & =54+4-12 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188069 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f512d235-f663-502f-bd8c-6b3b6748913b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Three Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "d849af65-721a-5a47-b8b7-9446e77046f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-10447" :question/problem "For three random variables $X_1,X_2,$ and $X_3,$ we have the following variances and covariances:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X_1] = 1,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Var}[X_2] = 3,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Var}[X_3] = 8   \\qquad\n$$\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X_1,X_2] = 2,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Cov}[X_1,X_3] = 4,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Cov}[X_2,X_3] = -5   \\qquad\n$$\n\nFind $\\textrm{Var}[5X_1 + 2X_2 + 3X_3].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1, \\ldots, X_n$ are random variables, and $a_1, \\ldots, a_n$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\left[\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} a_i X_i \\right]\n= \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} a_i^2 \\textrm{Var}[X_i] + 2\\sum\\limits_{i <     j} a_i a_j \\textrm{Cov}[X_i,X_j].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[5{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+3{X}_{3}] & ={5}^{2}\\cdot 1+{2}^{2}\\cdot 3+{3}^{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 5\\cdot 2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 5\\cdot 3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =25+12+72+40+120-60 \\\\  & =209.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188357 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91379d24-6b6d-5642-8eb8-cbcc8feaf355" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum or Difference of Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3ab039-cc62-5351-99fd-6a146e32f748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186961} {:answer/id #uuid "03dae12c-a476-54ba-8470-c815fbc216d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186962} {:answer/id #uuid "2a365b07-d561-504a-b178-b01a6cd3917b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186963} {:answer/id #uuid "6097cc51-f3dd-5304-aea7-f4b903e0c7c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186964} {:answer/id #uuid "681b7828-21bd-5e1e-a0e2-c156e50dab57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6097cc51-f3dd-5304-aea7-f4b903e0c7c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186964} :answer-field/id #uuid "449289da-9cff-5a2e-82d1-d38f2cb079bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d5f1713-8427-52de-a536-09c214fa1b7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-148153" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=7,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=5,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=3.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=7+5+2\\cdot 3=18.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188359 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96172470-bd90-53eb-aea7-87d08f462ea2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Scaled Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a267d2c0-8cef-5419-8bd8-6b124b79e2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "71" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186979} {:answer/id #uuid "058b34fc-e14b-5117-9c4b-12046392c4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186980} {:answer/id #uuid "14e8a042-fb53-5771-bbb2-185cce6f53f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186981} {:answer/id #uuid "742a8e57-aae3-5909-942c-bbd923e158ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "101" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186982} {:answer/id #uuid "78c57dac-f765-52f2-8300-939b66f45f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a267d2c0-8cef-5419-8bd8-6b124b79e2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "71" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186979} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ee6dc71-a0fa-5cf9-8151-0278d7f8c697" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd21e11d-cee2-5d23-9e71-322494488f5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-148156" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=5,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=11,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=4.$ Find $\\text{Var}[2X-3Y].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-3Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-3)^{2}\\cdot 11+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20+99-48 \\\\  & =71.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f512d235-f663-502f-bd8c-6b3b6748913b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Three Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd1f23c2-6747-51ae-9f60-02581263b363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "205" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186985} {:answer/id #uuid "dc18f794-d6f6-5049-812e-926da1a335e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186986} {:answer/id #uuid "56d68d7b-ded6-520a-aade-538a0d2bca4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "185" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186987} {:answer/id #uuid "57b2e6c4-761b-5a3d-93ce-e1293de5f8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "165" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186988} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1dcffa-fe6e-51b1-8c80-ed9e58cbe8ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "195" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56d68d7b-ded6-520a-aade-538a0d2bca4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "185" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186987} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c634ce-1efc-5440-bac3-81ca5c4d1a4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4c20916-66f7-5f38-b102-b5a620d22dbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-148160" :question/problem "For three random variables ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3},$ we have the following variances and covariances:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]=5,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]=4,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}]=2\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]=3,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]=1,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]=2\\,\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+4{X}_{3}].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},…,{X}_{n}$ are random variables, and ${a}_{1},…,{a}_{n}$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{X}_{i}]={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{i}]+2{\\sum }_{i<j}{a}_{i}{a}_{j}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{i},{X}_{j}].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+4{X}_{3}] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 4+{4}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =45+16+32+36+24+32 \\\\  & =185.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39efc83e-6658-5b7a-979b-dbc35af5dd98" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f0a5ae0-3d3b-5b19-894e-01a395a7908b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186997} {:answer/id #uuid "00611cca-0cb0-545e-9550-a63764016e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186998} {:answer/id #uuid "3f554486-3123-5996-85ee-1e07917d7202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186999} {:answer/id #uuid "6ded9c5e-2336-5d95-b9c6-ace0e17aad0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187000} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd0bd3f-7b73-5f7c-8613-cdf6a15724c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f0a5ae0-3d3b-5b19-894e-01a395a7908b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186997} :answer-field/id #uuid "449f3f8d-204c-5706-983a-90f6e3af463d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf786f34-fcab-562f-85da-9ff62292e23b" :question/math-academy-id "q-148162" :question/problem "Consider two random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=2,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=4,$ mixed moment $\\text{E}[XY]=10,$ and second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=9$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=20.$ Find the variance of $2X-5Y.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =9-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =20-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =10-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-5Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-5)^{2}\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =20+100-40 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39efc83e-6658-5b7a-979b-dbc35af5dd98" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8657b45e-47a1-5e07-a754-bec6f64f93c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.82" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187003} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e8190f-d025-57eb-98d5-e9bc0d004dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187004} {:answer/id #uuid "3db4b967-cbcd-5a79-b087-e24125d749ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187005} {:answer/id #uuid "50bbe0a7-1060-5131-91f7-74c3387b1491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187006} {:answer/id #uuid "60587763-da89-56a6-852e-d0aa1b200af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7e8190f-d025-57eb-98d5-e9bc0d004dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187004} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2f4fd58-de6a-55be-876b-52e504d4c3f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa43e91a-459b-5961-9f5d-0107414a7dce" :question/math-academy-id "q-148163" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[2X+3Y].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | $0.8$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.2+1\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =0.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.2+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.8-{0.8}^{2} \\\\  & =0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =1.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 0.4+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2.8-{1.6}^{2} \\\\  & =0.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We compute $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+1\\cdot 1\\cdot f(1,1)+1\\cdot 2\\cdot f(1,2) \\\\  & =0+0+1\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.3-0.8\\cdot 1.6 \\\\  & =0.02.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X+3Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 0.16+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.24+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot 0.02 \\\\  & =0.64+2.16+0.24 \\\\  & =3.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188357 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91379d24-6b6d-5642-8eb8-cbcc8feaf355" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum or Difference of Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1447dd96-4c0d-5c24-b2d3-b8448373e4c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526543} {:answer/id #uuid "3480cd1d-522b-51c3-a913-a3671a5b2050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526603} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe36719-579c-5bc3-ba9d-1a7681221763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526665} {:answer/id #uuid "b36db42d-1df7-5939-8117-91241e0857be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526845} {:answer/id #uuid "e97f786f-3f8e-5534-bb52-d041c29138ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e97f786f-3f8e-5534-bb52-d041c29138ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526966} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb090ab1-dbc9-5b97-ac8f-d7e17a3c0dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3e39928-eadb-5eb3-9eda-f3457f0505b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-148304" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.64,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=2.56,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.48.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=0.64+2.56+2\\cdot 0.48=4.16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188357 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91379d24-6b6d-5642-8eb8-cbcc8feaf355" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum or Difference of Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b5b6e8f-5bc3-560d-8885-95ce43bf6cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526715} {:answer/id #uuid "b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526842} {:answer/id #uuid "d00ac744-2b33-547b-8327-668720b71a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526902} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d75129-0300-58cb-992b-b2f66d1dd767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526963} {:answer/id #uuid "f787f52b-7c28-5038-948b-07653cdbb173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526842} :answer-field/id #uuid "d797f9f7-f609-5c5e-ba78-717e24c03bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bade78ae-2b02-5df2-9480-36d57f4806a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-148307" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{8},$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{3}{4},$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\frac{5}{16}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{3}{4}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{16}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527189 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188357 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91379d24-6b6d-5642-8eb8-cbcc8feaf355" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum or Difference of Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a81e4ece-d7f2-5c11-822e-db92a71d403c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526828} {:answer/id #uuid "c23cc5cc-232d-50cb-bf03-dcc14216ffbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526872} {:answer/id #uuid "cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526897} {:answer/id #uuid "d440fa76-ed34-5fa7-ba1a-4299f3912c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526910} {:answer/id #uuid "eeac769e-1c7d-5f17-9702-eee8738c6039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526897} :answer-field/id #uuid "98eba2e3-746d-555e-a1fb-96940568baf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0026095-8676-593f-8d69-3fa08a38ef1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-148310" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=4,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=1,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=1.2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=4+1-2\\cdot 1.2=2.6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188357 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91379d24-6b6d-5642-8eb8-cbcc8feaf355" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum or Difference of Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "481038a8-d449-5b39-8dda-544960d7f632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526644} {:answer/id #uuid "9f578386-a3d2-544b-abed-42030e1016dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526809} {:answer/id #uuid "bafd273d-ce56-5258-8a54-032916d858c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526860} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f70f08-c5c2-55d3-9f31-b5f42ea6e420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526968} {:answer/id #uuid "f957552d-c41f-567d-88a0-ad5c32655218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f957552d-c41f-567d-88a0-ad5c32655218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526997} :answer-field/id #uuid "37059df0-2019-5852-bef9-67f5bbc9e447" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94546e94-1af9-54e7-9a1b-29fb0570cfc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-148315" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{7}{4},$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{5}{2},$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\frac{3}{4}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{5}{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188359 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96172470-bd90-53eb-aea7-87d08f462ea2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Scaled Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b0f9e8-5bed-5e28-8aa4-8891548dbee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526537} {:answer/id #uuid "25c6b3fe-797b-5c3b-b5d3-ad2fbd9060da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526586} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b45f6f-0aca-5265-a86f-dc576861c0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526879} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f45a7c-cd89-5de7-919f-40df36a8e57e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526967} {:answer/id #uuid "fb52047a-64f1-55c6-bcdc-b7d871b74bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9f45a7c-cd89-5de7-919f-40df36a8e57e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526967} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9903df-3d0e-558c-a936-1e634a7a414f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "079f02ad-9ee0-58ac-bead-d4394104b125" :question/math-academy-id "q-148325" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=2,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=4,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=3.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X+2Y] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 2+{2}^{2}\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =2+16+12 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188359 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96172470-bd90-53eb-aea7-87d08f462ea2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Scaled Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042d7ca6-0980-5b74-8fb1-e853458aefff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526510} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe11208-1cf5-5ebb-b9ae-1cfd9d864264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526574} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed17f21-46a7-5c9d-badf-51e6f9909dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526623} {:answer/id #uuid "5212a1f4-14ce-5363-9b60-7fca91d0f9cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526667} {:answer/id #uuid "5b321d10-02bd-5f8b-9dc8-387f61a077be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "042d7ca6-0980-5b74-8fb1-e853458aefff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526510} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a50128-f069-562c-b225-44f83d8c3770" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d139a777-1244-5988-9682-4e7da954d933" :question/math-academy-id "q-148329" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=3,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=5,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=1.$ Find $\\text{Var}[3X-4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-4Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-4)^{2}\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =27+80-24 \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188359 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96172470-bd90-53eb-aea7-87d08f462ea2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Scaled Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1730b466-edec-5557-8be0-4765900d97d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526550} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdc858f-23d2-52f7-803a-0d8ca2c80206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526616} {:answer/id #uuid "60036dd0-65af-52cb-a069-bd37caf7adfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526695} {:answer/id #uuid "909907e4-2fff-5429-908d-172891d594e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526788} {:answer/id #uuid "a7330edf-fd61-584c-a0ef-021af49ab7e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7330edf-fd61-584c-a0ef-021af49ab7e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526824} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2574087-a149-5760-a3e0-95a498fe4957" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e6dcf9d-d6cd-51ac-b73d-58cf9701a199" :question/math-academy-id "q-148330" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.24,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.06,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.08.$ Find $\\text{Var}[2X-8Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-8Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 0.24+(-8)^{2}\\cdot 0.06+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-8)\\cdot 0.08 \\\\  & =0.96+3.84-2.56 \\\\  & =2.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188359 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96172470-bd90-53eb-aea7-87d08f462ea2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Scaled Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13b69179-3383-516b-9efb-08040395b10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526541} {:answer/id #uuid "2feeb232-e56f-552c-962e-5f79343f3fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526595} {:answer/id #uuid "4a635d19-edad-56dc-9f3e-8fb6e159993d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526654} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526694} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a635d19-edad-56dc-9f3e-8fb6e159993d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526654} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e79e9c9-3fca-53e4-af45-03318ed7bb0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-148331" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.1,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.7,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[7X-4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X-4Y] & ={7}^{2}\\cdot 0.1+(-4)^{2}\\cdot 0.7+2\\cdot 7\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =4.9+11.2-11.2 \\\\  & =4.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39efc83e-6658-5b7a-979b-dbc35af5dd98" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468fa4dd-aa55-5c1c-adbf-af8f95c32adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526639} {:answer/id #uuid "49ada7d0-4cef-56d8-bcef-b0502f40aca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.69" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526651} {:answer/id #uuid "5470918e-e06a-57bb-b01a-7b0ef04bc1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526675} {:answer/id #uuid "720fce8b-4a4c-5001-875c-151d8e621507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526725} {:answer/id #uuid "8b1cefcd-2445-53e0-9e6c-8133a9228e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b1cefcd-2445-53e0-9e6c-8133a9228e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526782} :answer-field/id #uuid "338abd00-bef7-5a0e-90d2-b18f076c9de2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "43034259-a22b-5dd7-b48f-a2ed42e0b13d" :question/math-academy-id "q-148346" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.7 \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.3+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.7 \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =2.8-{1.4}^{2} \\\\  & =0.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =0.5-{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot f(0,0)+0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+2\\cdot 0\\cdot f(2,0)+2\\cdot 1\\cdot f(2,1) \\\\  & =0+0+0+2\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =0.6-1.4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 0.84+(-1)^{2}\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-0.1) \\\\  & =7.56+0.25+0.6 \\\\  & =8.41.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39efc83e-6658-5b7a-979b-dbc35af5dd98" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "070e6987-47d6-5f73-9aa9-86a2d5cb82ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526517} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9906a6-c4a0-571b-a9fe-b0988e41fc63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526626} {:answer/id #uuid "7f42f492-9fe9-5724-b584-66ae829fc7d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526754} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d64e3b-21c0-551e-b123-974f1cbd894d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526827} {:answer/id #uuid "e7dcec73-2add-5548-aec0-fc739525b3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f9906a6-c4a0-571b-a9fe-b0988e41fc63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526626} :answer-field/id #uuid "e551be10-49d7-5b00-a0da-a0e8ce37b373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e96228aa-7e46-5ce5-96d2-d22e87559f00" :question/math-academy-id "q-148348" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3X-2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.55+2\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.55+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =1.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =1.8-{0.9}^{2} \\\\  & =0.99.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2.5-{1.5}^{2} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+2\\cdot 1\\cdot f(2,1)+2\\cdot 2\\cdot f(2,2) \\\\  & =0+0+2\\cdot 0.2+4\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.4-0.9\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & =0.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X-2Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 0.99+(-2)^{2}\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0.05 \\\\  & =8.91+1-0.6 \\\\  & =9.31.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188360 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39efc83e-6658-5b7a-979b-dbc35af5dd98" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e3129f4-5fbf-5a1b-8819-be0cbbf448d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526594} {:answer/id #uuid "b594c8db-9430-5a22-b797-08e58983a322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526851} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3807e9-784b-5046-9fb0-1d5c63a1fe7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43.86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526861} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b3b1e0-de02-59a0-8905-c06056522de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39.62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526886} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7482b1-371a-5ba6-941f-1144ea4bfa78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb7482b1-371a-5ba6-941f-1144ea4bfa78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526970} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4a349e6-751b-52e3-889b-23f3be2178b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c291da1-e168-5e62-8128-2d4c3d94af53" :question/math-academy-id "q-148351" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[3X+4Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.55$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.45+4\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =2.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.45+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =8.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =8.8-{2.2}^{2} \\\\  & =3.96.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2.5-{1.5}^{2} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+4\\cdot 1\\cdot f(4,1)+4\\cdot 2\\cdot f(4,2) \\\\  & =0+0+4\\cdot 0.2+8\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =3.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =3.6-2.2\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X+4Y] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 3.96+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =35.64+4+7.2 \\\\  & =46.84.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188361 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f512d235-f663-502f-bd8c-6b3b6748913b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum of Three Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78534fc9-e405-57b5-9b6d-30c8b94d0b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "209" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526738} {:answer/id #uuid "83f959c6-ecaf-52c2-83d2-c523d4096a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "185" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526767} {:answer/id #uuid "845e1070-adec-50b4-baf7-02a5443b23d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526768} {:answer/id #uuid "a508ac9a-d3b2-5d7e-9955-803b8f2e995c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "217" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526817} {:answer/id #uuid "f22af125-b5c3-5190-b0ab-21b1cca3cf1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "196" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78534fc9-e405-57b5-9b6d-30c8b94d0b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "209" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526738} :answer-field/id #uuid "7013aeae-6a4b-54c0-a7ce-c4c928ca841d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0b47f27-b72b-520b-9e5b-9f7678a818fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-148399" :question/problem "For three random variables ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},$ and ${X}_{3},$ we have the following variances and covariances:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]=3,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]=0.5,\\,\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}]=1.5\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]=-0.75,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]=-3.5,\\,\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]=4\\,\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}+4{X}_{2}+6{X}_{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},…,{X}_{n}$ are random variables, and ${a}_{1},…,{a}_{n}$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{X}_{i}]={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{a}_{i}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{i}]+2{\\sum }_{i<j}{a}_{i}{a}_{j}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{i},{X}_{j}].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}+4{X}_{2}+6{X}_{3}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 3+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{6}^{2}\\cdot 1.5 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 1\\cdot 4\\cdot (-0.75)+2\\cdot 1\\cdot 6\\cdot (-3.5)+2\\cdot 4\\cdot 6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =3+8+54-6-42+192 \\\\  & =209.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
